
<svelte:head><title>Article request privacy | Stepan Kukharskiy</title><link rel="canonical" href="https://stepankukharskiy.com/ai-work/privacy" /></svelte:head>
<h1>Article request counts</h1><p>I count eligible requests for the Excel-to-PowerPoint article to understand interest in the experiment. The server logs only the UTC day, fixed article/Skill identifier, event type and a fixed personal-site or Medium campaign label.</p>
<p>These event records contain no visitor identifiers, IP addresses, cookies, referrers, user-agent strings, raw URLs or work content. Headers are checked in memory to omit common bots, prefetch, Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control requests. No analytics cookies, fingerprinting or browser tracking scripts are used. The server setting <code>PERSONAL_WEBSITE_ANALYTICS=off</code> disables these counts.</p>
<p>A request is not a unique reader, completed download, installation or Skill execution. Repeat requests and unrecognized bots can affect totals. Relay counts its own page and download requests separately; no person-level linking is performed.</p>
<p>Railway hosts this site and may process connection metadata and operational logs under <a href="https://railway.com/legal/privacy">its privacy policy</a>. No additional analytics service or database is configured, and no fixed hosting-log retention period is promised. <a href="https://task-relay-website-production.up.railway.app/skills/privacy">Relay's website privacy details</a>.</p>
